# Title
Preserve red-pair dependency order for NEW-module oracles in _enforce_module_first

# Scope
EDIT the EXISTING file `harness/planner/plan_normalizer.py` (READ it first).
SINGLE FILE — emit a `__JANUSMASK_PATCHES__` SYMBOL patch replacing ONLY
`_enforce_module_first`. Sensitive path, so the impl task is `harness_self_fix`.
The fix: in the carve-out (currently ~lines 173-179), DROP the `is_file()` on-disk
existence check AND the now-unused `repo_root is not None` guard, so the carve-out
fires whenever the impl's `verification_command` substring-names one of THIS
oracle's `files_touched` test files. Everything else (the `oracle`/`impl` pairing,
the flip block, the acyclic-fixup `while` loop) stays byte-identical.

# Inputs
READ `harness/planner/plan_normalizer.py::_enforce_module_first`. VERIFIED current
bug: for a NEW-module red-pair (a `test_authoring` oracle whose `mutation_target`
names a module the impl CREATES), the carve-out's `(Path(repo_root)/_module_path(target)).is_file()`
is False, so the carve-out is skipped and the flip sets `oracle.deps=[impl]`,
`impl.deps=[]` — the deadlock direction (impl fires first, runs the not-yet-authored
test, fails). The impl's vc NAMING the oracle's authored test IS the definitive
fix-forward signal; module-on-disk is irrelevant. Sibling sanitizer
`_sanitize_impl_verification_commands` (~:268-290) already keys its own red-pair
guard on the same vc-names-test signal WITHOUT an is_file() check. Runtime
acceptance for new-module RED oracles is `orchestrator._new_module_red_by_absence`
(direction-agnostic), so preserving `impl.deps=[oracle]` is safe. The RED oracle
below is the source of truth.

# Non-Goals
Integration is out of scope (the word `integration` MUST appear here to excuse the
integration-test requirement). Do NOT touch any other symbol, function, or file. Do
NOT widen the carve-out to fire when the impl vc does NOT name an oracle test file
(a genuine non-red-pair must STILL be flipped to module-first). Do NOT alter
`is_fix_forward_redpair` or any orchestrator/acceptance code.

# Deliverables
`harness/planner/plan_normalizer.py` with `_enforce_module_first` preserving the
correct red-pair direction for NEW-module oracles, GREEN under the scoped
verification_command, with no regression to existing-module or non-red-pair behavior.

# Required plan shape
EXACTLY TWO tasks. Oracle depends on impl is FORBIDDEN; the impl depends on the oracle.

