- meta_task_type: test_authoring
- mutation_target: `harness.planner.plan_normalizer`
- files_touched: ["tests/harness/test_redpair_newmodule_order.py"]
- dependencies: []
- verification_command: `python -m pytest tests/harness/test_redpair_newmodule_order.py -q`
- The oracle AUTHORS `tests/harness/test_redpair_newmodule_order.py` (submit as
  ordinary Python — NOT importlib; `normalize_plan` is existing harness code,
  import it directly: `from harness.planner.plan_normalizer import normalize_plan`).
  The test MUST be data-driven (no hardcoded answer-key; no clock/uuid/random/network)
  and MUST contain at least these three assertions:
  1. NEW-MODULE RED-PAIR (the bug): build a 2-task plan in memory — a
     `test_authoring` oracle (mutation_target `pkg.newmod`, files_touched
     `["tests/pkg/test_newmod.py"]`, dependencies `[]`, vcmd
     `python -m pytest tests/pkg/test_newmod.py -q`) and an impl
