     oracle's test). Call `normalize_plan(plan, repo_root=str(tmp_path))` where
     `tmp_path` is an empty dir so `pkg/newmod.py` is ABSENT. Assert the surviving
     oracle's `dependencies == []` AND the impl's `dependencies == [oracle_id]`.
     (RED today: currently inverted to oracle.deps=[impl], impl.deps=[]; GREEN after fix.)
  2. NON-VACUITY / NARROWNESS REGRESSION: the SAME plan but the impl's vcmd names an
     UNRELATED test (NOT the oracle's file), module still ABSENT → assert the result
     is STILL inverted (oracle.deps==[impl_id], impl.deps==[]). This proves the fix
